.env
*.env
!.env.example

# Runtime caches. Never commit either of these.
#
# cache/ holds controller snapshots: a MAC, hostname and IP inventory of every
# device on the network. Regenerable with `unifi-map fetch`.
#
# It also holds Ubiquiti's device catalog and downloaded product artwork.
# That artwork is Ubiquiti's intellectual property and is deliberately NOT
# vendored into this repository; it is fetched at runtime and cached locally.
# Snapshots and renders. The glob matters: a snapshot is a full inventory of a
# network (every MAC, hostname, address and SSID), and the obvious thing to do
# before a risky fetch is `cp -r cache cache.bak`, which `cache/` alone does not
# cover. That exact backup sat untracked in this repository once, one `git add
# -A` away from being published.
cache*/
out*/

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Editor scratch files
*.sw[a-p]
*~
.*.swp
